📌 date_extract
    Extracts dates from text.
    Supports formats like DD/MM/YYYY, MM-DD-YYYY, YYYY.MM.DD.
    Useful for log analysis and text mining.
    Uses regex to detect numeric + separator-based date patterns.


📌 email_extract
    Extracts email addresses from text.
    Works with formats like example@gmail.com, user.name@domain.co.in.
    Helps in data cleaning, scraping, and contact extraction.
    Uses regex to match [username]@[domain].[extension].


📌 hashtag_extract 
    Extracts hashtags (e.g., #Python, #AI).
    Supports alphanumeric hashtags with underscores.
    Useful for social media analysis.
    Regex ensures # followed by word characters is matched.


📌 phone_number
    Extracts phone numbers in different formats.
    Examples: +91-9876543210, (123)-456-7890, 9876543210.
    Useful for building contact scrapers.
    Regex checks for optional country codes and separators.


📌 url_extract
    Extracts URLs from text.
    Works with http, https, and www links.
    Examples: https://example.com, www.google.com.
    Helpful in web scraping and link validation.